# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow works like a Python function that runs on remote compute. Compare a local function with the same code as a workflow:\n"
msgstr "Gumagana ang managed workflow na parang Python function na tumatakbo sa remote compute. Ihambing ang isang local function sa parehong code bilang workflow:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`Local Python`**\n"
msgstr "**`Local Python`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a managed workflow, `run()` is the call, `get_arguments()` gives the workflow its parameters, and `save_result()` is its `return` statement. Because the workflow runs as a separate job on remote compute, it differs from a local function call in three ways:\n"
msgstr "Sa isang managed workflow, ang `run()` ang tawag, ang `get_arguments()` ang nagbibigay sa workflow ng mga parameter nito, at ang `save_result()` ang `return` statement nito. Dahil tumatakbo ang workflow bilang hiwalay na job sa remote compute, naiiba ito sa local function call sa tatlong paraan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The client encodes arguments and results.** Each value must be one that the client can encode, and some types change. See [Read arguments in your workflow](#read-arguments-in-your-workflow).\n"
msgstr "**Ine-encode ng client ang mga argument at resulta.** Dapat ang bawat value ay isang kayang i-encode ng client, at may mga type na nagbabago. Tingnan ang [Basahin ang mga argument sa workflow mo](#read-arguments-in-your-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The call does not wait.** `run()` returns a job immediately, and you read the result later with `job.result()`. See [Save results](#save-results).\n"
msgstr "**Hindi naghihintay ang tawag.** Agad na nagbabalik ng job ang `run()`, at babasahin mo ang resulta sa ibang pagkakataon gamit ang `job.result()`. Tingnan ang [I-save ang mga resulta](#save-results).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Nothing checks the call.** A Python function rejects an unknown keyword argument, but a workflow ignores it unless you attach a schema. See [Best practice: validate arguments with a schema](#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema).\n"
msgstr "**Walang sumusuri sa tawag.** Tinatanggihan ng Python function ang hindi kilalang keyword argument, pero binabalewala ito ng workflow maliban kung maglakip ka ng schema. Tingnan ang [Best practice: i-validate ang mga argument gamit ang schema](#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Your local notebook, run_workflow_remotely.ipynb, calls run(args). A workflow runs an optional schema check, then creates the managed workflow job, source_files/my_workflow.py. The job reads its arguments with get_arguments(), runs your code, such as mapping, transpiling circuits, running primitives, and post-processing, and returns a result with save_result(). A workflow stores the result, and your notebook reads it with job.result().](/docs/images/managed-workflows/inputs-outputs.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Your local notebook, run_workflow_remotely.ipynb, calls run(args). A workflow runs an optional schema check, then creates the managed workflow job, source_files/my_workflow.py. The job reads its arguments with get_arguments(), runs your code, such as mapping, transpiling circuits, running primitives, and post-processing, and returns a result with save_result(). A workflow stores the result, and your notebook reads it with job.result().](/docs/images/managed-workflows/inputs-outputs.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read arguments in your workflow {#read-arguments-in-your-workflow}"
msgstr "Basahin ang mga argument sa workflow mo {#read-arguments-in-your-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass inputs to your workflow from your local notebook:\n"
msgstr "Magpasa ng mga input sa workflow mo mula sa local notebook mo:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, edit your workflow code to fetch arguments with `get_arguments()`, which returns a dictionary whose keys are the argument names:\n"
msgstr "Para magawa ito, i-edit ang code ng workflow mo para kunin ang mga argument gamit ang `get_arguments()`, na nagbabalik ng dictionary na ang mga key ay ang mga pangalan ng argument:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The dictionary contains only the arguments that the run passed, so use `arguments.get()` with a default value for optional arguments. You can use any argument name except the protected keywords `config` and `function_size`, because `run()` uses these keywords directly. `run()` also rejects `compute_profile`. To choose compute resources, pass `function_size`.\n"
msgstr "Naglalaman lang ang dictionary ng mga argument na ipinasa ng run, kaya gamitin ang `arguments.get()` na may default na value para sa mga opsyonal na argument. Puwede kang gumamit ng kahit anong pangalan ng argument maliban sa mga protektadong keyword na `config` at `function_size`, dahil direktang ginagamit ng `run()` ang mga keyword na ito. Tinatanggihan din ng `run()` ang `compute_profile`. Para pumili ng compute resources, ipasa ang `function_size`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To read the size that the job runs at, call `get_function_size()` in your workflow code:\n"
msgstr "Para basahin ang laki kung saan tumatakbo ang job, tawagin ang `get_function_size()` sa code ng workflow mo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the run does not pass `function_size`, `get_function_size()` returns the workflow's default size. See [Choose a size for each run](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#choose-a-size-for-each-run).\n"
msgstr "Kung hindi nagpasa ng `function_size` ang run, ibinabalik ng `get_function_size()` ang default na laki ng workflow. Tingnan ang [Pumili ng laki para sa bawat run](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#choose-a-size-for-each-run).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supported argument types {#supported-argument-types}"
msgstr "Mga suportadong uri ng argument {#supported-argument-types}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each value must be JSON-serializable, or an object that the client can encode, such as a Qiskit circuit or a NumPy array. Because the client encodes each argument before it sends the job and `get_arguments()` decodes it inside the workflow, the workflow receives the original Python object.\n"
msgstr "Dapat JSON-serializable ang bawat value, o isang object na kayang i-encode ng client, gaya ng Qiskit circuit o NumPy array. Dahil ine-encode ng client ang bawat argument bago ipadala ang job at dine-decode ito ng `get_arguments()` sa loob ng workflow, natatanggap ng workflow ang orihinal na Python object.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The client sends `int`, `float`, `str`, `bool`, `None`, and lists or dictionaries of these unchanged. It encodes other objects, such as a `QuantumCircuit`, a `numpy.ndarray`, or a `complex` number, as a dictionary with a `__type__` tag and a `__value__`. You need this form when you [write an argument schema](#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema).\n"
msgstr "Ipinapadala ng client nang walang pagbabago ang `int`, `float`, `str`, `bool`, `None`, at mga list o dictionary ng mga ito. Ine-encode nito ang iba pang object, gaya ng `QuantumCircuit`, `numpy.ndarray`, o `complex` na numero, bilang dictionary na may `__type__` tag at `__value__`. Kailangan mo ang anyong ito kapag [sumusulat ka ng argument schema](#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because JSON has no equivalent for some types, these types change during encoding. Tuples arrive as lists, dictionary keys arrive as strings, and NumPy integers such as `np.int64` arrive as `int`. If the client cannot encode a value, such as `bytes` or `np.float32`, `run()` raises a `TypeError` and does not create a job.\n"
msgstr "Dahil walang katumbas sa JSON ang ilang type, nagbabago ang mga type na ito habang ine-encode. Dumarating bilang list ang mga tuple, dumarating bilang string ang mga dictionary key, at dumarating bilang `int` ang mga NumPy integer gaya ng `np.int64`. Kung hindi ma-encode ng client ang isang value, gaya ng `bytes` o `np.float32`, nagtataas ang `run()` ng `TypeError` at hindi gumagawa ng job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some objects cannot be passed as arguments. For example, pass a backend's name as a string instead of a `Backend` object, and create the backend inside the workflow. See [Run quantum jobs from a workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows).\n"
msgstr "Hindi maipapasa bilang argument ang ilang object. Halimbawa, ipasa ang pangalan ng backend bilang string sa halip na `Backend` object, at likhain ang backend sa loob ng workflow. Tingnan ang [Magpatakbo ng mga quantum job mula sa workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Size limits {#size-limits}"
msgstr "Mga limitasyon sa laki {#size-limits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The arguments of one run can be up to 32 MB after encoding. For example, one 100-qubit circuit with a depth of 100 encodes to about 39 KB, so a single run can take a batch of about 800 such circuits. For larger inputs, [upload a file](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) and pass its name as an argument.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga argument ng isang run ay hanggang 32 MB pagkatapos ma-encode. Halimbawa, ang isang 100-qubit na circuit na may depth na 100 ay nag-e-encode sa humigit-kumulang 39 KB, kaya ang isang run ay kayang kumuha ng batch ng humigit-kumulang 800 ganoong circuit. Para sa mas malalaking input, [mag-upload ng file](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) at ipasa ang pangalan nito bilang argument.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: 32 MB is MAX_ARGUMENTS_LENGTH_MB, which is checked when the workflow declares a schema. The 50 MB request body limit applies to every run. Confirm the number to publish. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save results {#save-results}"
msgstr "I-save ang mga resulta {#save-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `save_result()` at the end of your workflow to return a result to your notebook. Read the result in your notebook with `job.result()`:\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang `save_result()` sa dulo ng workflow mo para magbalik ng resulta sa notebook mo. Basahin ang resulta sa notebook mo gamit ang `job.result()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, call `save_result()` in your workflow code:\n"
msgstr "Para magawa ito, tawagin ang `save_result()` sa code ng workflow mo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`save_result()` encodes the result in the same way that the client encodes arguments, and `job.result()` decodes it. A result can therefore contain the [supported argument types](#supported-argument-types), such as circuits, NumPy arrays, and the result of a primitive job, with the same type changes.\n"
msgstr "Ine-encode ng `save_result()` ang resulta sa parehong paraan ng pag-encode ng client sa mga argument, at dine-decode ito ng `job.result()`. Kaya ang resulta ay puwedeng maglaman ng [mga suportadong uri ng argument](#supported-argument-types), gaya ng mga circuit, NumPy array, at resulta ng primitive job, na may parehong pagbabago sa type.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Check the return value.** If `save_result()` cannot encode the value, it logs a warning and returns `False` instead of raising an error. Without a check, the job can end with the `DONE` status and no result.\n"
msgstr "**Suriin ang return value.** Kung hindi ma-encode ng `save_result()` ang value, nagla-log ito ng babala at nagbabalik ng `False` sa halip na magtaas ng error. Kapag walang pagsusuri, puwedeng matapos ang job na may status na `DONE` at walang resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Only the last `save_result()` is stored.** Each call replaces the saved result. To return several values, save them in one dictionary, or write them to the logs.\n"
msgstr "**Ang huling `save_result()` lang ang iniimbak.** Pinapalitan ng bawat tawag ang naka-save na resulta. Para magbalik ng maraming value, i-save ang mga ito sa iisang dictionary, o isulat ang mga ito sa mga log.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**An empty dictionary means no result.** If the workflow never calls `save_result()`, `job.result()` returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "**Ang walang lamang dictionary ay nangangahulugang walang resulta.** Kung hindi kailanman tinawag ng workflow ang `save_result()`, nagbabalik ang `job.result()` ng `{}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To return files, such as large arrays or plots, save them to [file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) and return their names in the result.\n"
msgstr "Para magbalik ng mga file, gaya ng malalaking array o plot, i-save ang mga ito sa [file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) at ibalik ang mga pangalan nito sa resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: validate arguments with a schema {#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema}"
msgstr "Best practice: i-validate ang mga argument gamit ang schema {#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a best practice, attach a [JSON Schema](https://json-schema.org/) to every workflow that takes arguments. The schema describes the arguments that the workflow accepts, and the workflow checks the arguments of every run against it before it creates the job. If the arguments do not match, `run()` fails immediately with an error that names the bad field, and the workflow does not create a job. Without a schema, bad arguments reach the workflow after the job starts, and the workflow ignores a misspelled argument name.\n"
msgstr "Bilang best practice, maglakip ng [JSON Schema](https://json-schema.org/) sa bawat workflow na tumatanggap ng mga argument. Inilalarawan ng schema ang mga argument na tinatanggap ng workflow, at sinusuri ng workflow ang mga argument ng bawat run laban dito bago gumawa ng job. Kung hindi tumutugma ang mga argument, agad na pumapalya ang `run()` na may error na pinangangalanan ang maling field, at hindi gumagawa ng job ang workflow. Kapag walang schema, makararating ang maling mga argument sa workflow pagkatapos magsimula ang job, at binabalewala ng workflow ang maling baybay na pangalan ng argument.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the schema with `arguments_schema` when you upload the workflow. Pass a dictionary, not a JSON string:\n"
msgstr "Itakda ang schema gamit ang `arguments_schema` kapag ina-upload mo ang workflow. Magpasa ng dictionary, hindi JSON string:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the following points in mind when you write a schema:\n"
msgstr "Tandaan ang mga sumusunod na punto kapag sumusulat ka ng schema:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Describe the encoded form of Qiskit and NumPy objects.** The schema checks the arguments as the client sends them, so a circuit is an object such as `{\"__type__\": \"QuantumCircuit\", \"__value__\": \"<base64-encoded QPY>\"}`, not a string or an array. Check the `__type__` tag, and treat `__value__` as an opaque string. A schema that describes a circuit as a string rejects every valid run.\n"
msgstr "**Ilarawan ang encoded na anyo ng mga Qiskit at NumPy object.** Sinusuri ng schema ang mga argument ayon sa pagpapadala ng client, kaya ang circuit ay isang object gaya ng `{\"__type__\": \"QuantumCircuit\", \"__value__\": \"<base64-encoded QPY>\"}`, hindi string o array. Suriin ang `__type__` tag, at ituring ang `__value__` bilang opaque na string. Tinatanggihan ng schema na naglalarawan sa circuit bilang string ang bawat wastong run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Set `\"additionalProperties\": false`.** Without this setting, the workflow ignores a misspelled argument name, such as `shotz`, without a warning, and runs with its default value. Declare every argument that the workflow accepts before you enable this setting.\n"
msgstr "**Itakda ang `\"additionalProperties\": false`.** Kapag wala ang setting na ito, binabalewala ng workflow ang maling baybay na pangalan ng argument, gaya ng `shotz`, nang walang babala, at tumatakbo ito gamit ang default na value. Ideklara ang bawat argument na tinatanggap ng workflow bago mo i-enable ang setting na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Mark arguments as required.** Add each argument that the workflow reads without a default value to `required`.\n"
msgstr "**Markahan ang mga argument bilang required.** Idagdag sa `required` ang bawat argument na binabasa ng workflow nang walang default na value.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the arguments do not match the schema, the error message names the rule and the location of the bad value:\n"
msgstr "Kung hindi tumutugma ang mga argument sa schema, pinangangalanan ng mensahe ng error ang rule at ang lokasyon ng maling value:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A schema checks the type, shape, and range of each argument. A schema cannot check whether two valid arguments conflict, or whether a circuit fits a backend. Keep those checks in the workflow code.\n"
msgstr "Sinusuri ng schema ang type, hugis, at saklaw ng bawat argument. Hindi masusuri ng schema kung nagbabanggaan ang dalawang wastong argument, o kung kasya ang circuit sa isang backend. Panatilihin ang mga pagsusuring iyon sa code ng workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update or remove a schema {#update-or-remove-a-schema}"
msgstr "I-update o alisin ang schema {#update-or-remove-a-schema}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To replace the schema, set a new `arguments_schema` and upload the workflow again.\n"
msgstr "Para palitan ang schema, magtakda ng bagong `arguments_schema` at i-upload muli ang workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To remove the schema, upload the workflow with `arguments_schema={}`.\n"
msgstr "Para alisin ang schema, i-upload ang workflow na may `arguments_schema={}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you upload the workflow without `arguments_schema`, the workflow keeps the stored schema.\n"
msgstr "Kung ia-upload mo ang workflow nang walang `arguments_schema`, pinananatili ng workflow ang naka-imbak na schema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see the schema that is in effect, read `my_workflow.arguments_schema`. A value of `None` means that the workflow has no schema.\n"
msgstr "Para makita ang schema na may bisa, basahin ang `my_workflow.arguments_schema`. Ang value na `None` ay nangangahulugang walang schema ang workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check arguments before you run {#check-arguments-before-you-run}"
msgstr "Suriin ang mga argument bago ka magpatakbo {#check-arguments-before-you-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Call `validate_arguments()` to check a set of arguments against the schema without starting a job:\n"
msgstr "Tawagin ang `validate_arguments()` para suriin ang isang set ng mga argument laban sa schema nang hindi nagsisimula ng job:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the arguments are not valid, `validate_arguments()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException` with the same message that `run()` returns for those arguments. If the workflow has no schema, any arguments are valid. A valid result does not guarantee that `run()` succeeds, because `run()` also checks other limits, such as the number of active jobs.\n"
msgstr "Kung hindi wasto ang mga argument, nagtataas ang `validate_arguments()` ng `QiskitServerlessException` na may parehong mensahe na ibinabalik ng `run()` para sa mga argument na iyon. Kung walang schema ang workflow, wasto ang anumang argument. Hindi ginagarantiya ng wastong resulta na magtatagumpay ang `run()`, dahil sinusuri rin ng `run()` ang iba pang limitasyon, gaya ng bilang ng mga aktibong job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schema rules {#schema-rules}"
msgstr "Mga rule ng schema {#schema-rules}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow rejects the upload if the schema breaks any of the following rules:\n"
msgstr "Tinatanggihan ng managed workflow ang upload kung nilalabag ng schema ang alinman sa mga sumusunod na rule:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The schema can be up to 64 KiB, with up to 64 levels of nesting and up to 200 subschemas.\n"
msgstr "Ang schema ay puwedeng hanggang 64 KiB, na may hanggang 64 na antas ng nesting at hanggang 200 subschema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "References must point inside the same schema, such as `#/$defs/circuit`, and every reference must resolve. References to URLs or files are not allowed.\n"
msgstr "Dapat tumuro sa loob ng parehong schema ang mga reference, gaya ng `#/$defs/circuit`, at dapat ma-resolve ang bawat reference. Hindi pinapayagan ang mga reference sa mga URL o file.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The schema must be an object or a boolean.\n"
msgstr "Dapat object o boolean ang schema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Also avoid the following problems, which the upload does not catch:\n"
msgstr "Iwasan din ang mga sumusunod na problema, na hindi nahuhuli ng upload:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Nested quantifiers in `pattern`.** A pattern such as `^(a+)+$` can take a very long time to evaluate. A workflow stops validation after a CPU time limit and rejects the run. Write patterns without a quantifier around a group that already contains one, such as `^ibm_[a-z0-9_]{1,40}$`.\n"
msgstr "**Nested na quantifier sa `pattern`.** Ang pattern na gaya ng `^(a+)+$` ay puwedeng tumagal nang napakatagal bago ma-evaluate. Humihinto ang workflow sa pag-validate pagkatapos ng limitasyon sa CPU time at tinatanggihan ang run. Sumulat ng mga pattern na walang quantifier sa paligid ng grupong may laman nang quantifier, gaya ng `^ibm_[a-z0-9_]{1,40}$`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`false` as a schema.** The schema `false` rejects every run. To remove validation, use `{}`.\n"
msgstr "**Ang `false` bilang schema.** Tinatanggihan ng schema na `false` ang bawat run. Para tanggalin ang validation, gamitin ang `{}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot a schema {#troubleshoot-a-schema}"
msgstr "I-troubleshoot ang schema {#troubleshoot-a-schema}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Every run is rejected on a circuit argument. | The schema describes the circuit as a string or an array. Describe it as an object with a `__type__` tag. |\n"
"| Valid runs are rejected. | `additionalProperties` is `false`, and the schema does not declare an argument that the run passes. The error `path` names the argument. |\n"
"| Invalid runs are not rejected. | The workflow has no schema. Check `my_workflow.arguments_schema`. |\n"
"| No run is checked, although you set a schema. | The schema was passed as a JSON string. Pass a dictionary. |\n"
"| The upload fails with a `400` error. | The schema breaks one of the [schema rules](#schema-rules). |\n"
"| The error says that validation took too much CPU time. | A `pattern` has nested quantifiers. Rewrite the pattern. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Sanhi |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Tinatanggihan ang bawat run sa isang circuit argument. | Inilalarawan ng schema ang circuit bilang string o array. Ilarawan ito bilang object na may `__type__` tag. |\n"
"| Tinatanggihan ang mga wastong run. | Ang `additionalProperties` ay `false`, at hindi idineklara ng schema ang isang argument na ipinapasa ng run. Pinangangalanan ng `path` ng error ang argument. |\n"
"| Hindi tinatanggihan ang mga di-wastong run. | Walang schema ang workflow. Suriin ang `my_workflow.arguments_schema`. |\n"
"| Walang run na sinusuri, kahit nagtakda ka ng schema. | Ipinasa ang schema bilang JSON string. Magpasa ng dictionary. |\n"
"| Pumapalya ang upload na may `400` error. | Nilalabag ng schema ang isa sa mga [rule ng schema](#schema-rules). |\n"
"| Sinasabi ng error na masyadong maraming CPU time ang kinuha ng validation. | May nested na quantifier ang isang `pattern`. Isulat muli ang pattern. |\n"
